1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,790
When personal data leaks, the
law starts a clock.

2
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:08,150
Under GDPR, the regulator must hear from
you within seventy-two hours.

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,130
The Philippines' privacy commission:

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,130
also seventy-two.

5
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:15,010
And under NIS2, an early warning
is due in twenty-four.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,770
Each regulator wants specific facts:

7
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,850
what happened, whose data,
how many people,

8
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,310
and what you've done about it.

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,490
On day one, those facts are
scattered across tickets,

10
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,630
comments, Confluence pages and
people's heads.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,270
72 Hours is a Forge app for Jira
Service Management,

12
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,750
built for the privacy and security teams
who have to report a breach.

13
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,810
It tracks every legal deadline, gathers
the facts with their sources,

14
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:43,210
and drafts each notice, while
people make every decision.

15
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,150
It works in five steps:

16
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,410
detect, scope, evidence, notice, and file.

17
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:51,350
Step one: detect.

18
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:53,870
The team adds one label to the incident.

19
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,490
72 Hours starts the clock from the
moment the team became aware,

20
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:00,830
and leaves an internal note so they
can confirm that time.

21
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,370
Step two: scope.

22
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:05,630
A few quick answers, like where the
affected people live,

23
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:08,160
how many there are, and how serious it is,

24
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,690
decide which laws apply.

25
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,890
Every deadline lands on one
board, counting down.

26
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:16,210
Each one is calculated by code
from the law's own text.

27
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,370
Open it, and you see the exact
article it comes from.

28
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:21,170
Step three: evidence.

29
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:25,070
Press Assemble evidence, and Clerk,
the app's AI assistant,

30
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,310
reads the incident, its comments, linked
work and Confluence pages,

31
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,540
then drafts each fact the regulators need,

32
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,690
with its source.

33
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,690
Clerk runs on Claude, hosted by Atlassian,

34
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,570
so the data stays on the platform.

35
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,490
A person reviews every draft
and accepts it.

36
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:43,630
When a fact is still unknown, ask
the person who knows.

37
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:47,950
The question becomes a Jira task, and the
answer flows back into the evidence.

38
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,790
Step four: notice.

39
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,280
72 Hours drafts each regulator's
notice in Confluence,

40
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,960
with its sources and assumptions.

41
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:59,310
Sign-off unlocks only when every
required fact has been accepted.

42
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,950
Step five: file.

43
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,270
The team files with the regulator,
then records it here.

44
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:08,760
That clock stops, its reminders end, and the
audit trail keeps who did what,

45
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:09,710
and when.

46
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,670
72 Hours works across Atlassian too.

47
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,150
Ask Clerk in Rovo what's still missing.

48
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:18,670
Call the same tools from any
AI agent over MCP.

49
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:22,600
And through Teamwork Graph, it finds what the
people on the incident have been

50
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:26,390
working on, and publishes each notice's
status back to the graph.

51
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,850
Before a real breach, teams can
rehearse with a sample drill.

52
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,210
72 Hours.

53
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,260
Deadlines calculated by code.

54
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,810
Drafts written by AI.

55
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:36,590
Decisions made by people.

